510 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 259 0 R
/E (      Event management has become an essential activity in educational institutions, organizations, and communities where multiple events are conducted regularly. Traditional methods of managing events, such as manual record keeping or spreadsheet-based tracking, often lead to inefficiencies, data inconsistencies, and difficulties in monitoring participant attendance. These limitations highlight the need for a more organized and automated system that can simplify event planning, registration, and monitoring processes while ensuring accuracy and security.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
511 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 259 0 R
/E (To address these challenges, the proposed system introduces EVENTHUB, a secure and scalable role-based event management platform. The system enables administrators, organizers, and participants to interact through a unified web interface, allowing efficient event creation, registration, and monitoring. By integrating modern technologies such as QR code and RFID-based entry verification, the system ensures secure participant authentication and accurate attendance tracking. Overall, EVENTHUB aims to improve the efficiency, reliability, and user experience of event management through automation and centralized data management.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2 3]
>>
endobj
512 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 259 0 R
/T (CHAPTER 1 INTRODUCTION )
/E (CHAPTER 1 INTRODUCTION )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
513 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 259 0 R
/E (The EVENTHUB system is designed to provide a structured and role-based environment where different users can perform their specific tasks efficiently. Administrators have the authority to manage user accounts, monitor events, and maintain overall system operations. Event organizers are responsible for creating and managing event details, handling participant registrations, and ensuring that event activities are properly coordinated. Participants can easily browse available events, register online, and receive confirmation for their participation through the system.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
endobj
514 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 259 0 R
/E (Furthermore, the system focuses on improving the security and transparency of event participation through automated verification and monitoring mechanisms. The integration of QR code and RFID-based identification allows quick validation of participants during event entry, reducing manual verification and minimizing errors. In addition, the centralized database enables real-time data updates, efficient record management, and accurate report generation, making the system reliable and scalable for managing events in educational institutions and organizations.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7 8]
>>
endobj
515 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 260 0 R
/E (2)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
516 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 260 0 R
/E (Event management has traditionally been handled using manual procedures or fragmented digital tools, which often fail to meet the demands of modern event organization.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
517 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 260 0 R
/E (Event management plays an important role in organizing activities such as conferences, workshops, cultural programs, technical events, and social gatherings. Traditionally, these events were managed using manual methods like paper-based registrations, physical tickets, and direct communication, which required significant time and effort. As the number and size of events increased, these methods became inefficient and prone to errors such as data loss, duplicate entries, and poor coordination. The growing demand for organized and efficient event handling has created the need for digital solutions.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
518 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 260 0 R
/E (With the rapid development of web technologies and increased internet usage, event management has gradually shifted toward online platforms. Web-based systems enable organizers to publish event details, manage registrations, and communicate with participants more effectively. At the same time, users benefit from easy access to event information and online booking facilities. However, many existing systems lack proper security, scalability, and user-friendly design, limiting their effectiveness in handling large numbers of users and events.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
endobj
519 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 260 0 R
/E (To address these challenges, EVENTHUB is proposed as a secure and scalable event management system using full-stack technologies. The system provides a centralized platform where administrators can manage events and users can register and book tickets conveniently. By integrating modern frontend and backend technologies with secure authentication mechanisms, EVENTHUB aims to improve efficiency, reduce manual effort, and provide a reliable solution for managing events in a digital environment.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
endobj
520 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 260 0 R
/T (1.1 Background )
/E (1.1 Background )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
521 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 260 0 R
/T (1.2 Problem Statement )
/E (1.2 Problem Statement )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
522 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 261 0 R
/E (3)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
523 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 261 0 R
/E (The primary objective of the EVENTHUB project is to design and develop a centralized event management system that simplifies the overall process of organizing events. The system aims to replace traditional manual methods with a digital platform that automates event creation, registration, and ticket booking. By reducing manual effort, the system helps minimize errors and improves operational efficiency. This objective focuses on providing a reliable and well-structured solution for managing events of different types and scales. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [1 2]
>>
endobj
524 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 261 0 R
/E ( Activities such as participant registration, ticket distribution, attendance tracking, and communication are commonly managed through spreadsheets, paper forms, or isolated applications. These approaches consume significant time and effort and are highly susceptible to human errors, including incorrect data entry, duplication of records, and loss of important information. As events grow in size and complexity, managing large volumes of participant data becomes increasingly difficult, resulting in poor coordination and reduced overall efficiency.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
525 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 261 0 R
/E (Although several online event management platforms exist, many of them lack proper security and structured access control mechanisms. Inadequate separation between administrator and user functionalities can result in unauthorized access to sensitive data such as user details, event schedules, and booking records. The absence of strong authentication and authorization methods increases the risk of data breaches and misuse, which can reduce user confidence and limit the effectiveness of such systems in real-world applications.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
526 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 261 0 R
/E (Scalability and system adaptability further contribute to the challenges faced by event organizers. Several existing systems are not designed to handle a growing number of users or simultaneous access during peak periods, leading to slow performance, server overload, and system downtime. Additionally, limited customization options and the absence of real-time updates restrict the ability of organizers to modify event details, track bookings efficiently, and respond quickly to changes. These limitations highlight the need for a secure, scalable, and flexible event management platform like EVENTHUB, which can support efficient operations, ensure data security, and adapt to evolving organizational requirements.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [5 6 7]
>>
endobj
527 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 261 0 R
