/E (Laudon and Laudon discussed the role of management information systems in improving organizational efficiency through digital transformation. Their work emphasizes how information systems automate administrative tasks such as data handling, scheduling, and user management. In the context of event management, these systems provide a structured approach to organizing events, managing participants, and maintaining records efficiently. The study highlights the importance of centralized platforms in reducing manual workload and improving decision-making. However, the authors note that system effectiveness largely depends on proper security mechanisms and scalable architecture.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [1]
