601 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 270 0 R
/E (Another significant challenge is the lack of security, scalability, and real-time management capabilities in existing systems. Many systems do not implement proper role-based access control, allowing unauthorized users to access or modify sensitive event data. In addition, these systems are not designed to handle a growing number of users, resulting in slow performance and system failures during peak usage. The absence of real-time updates makes it difficult for organizers to monitor registrations, manage seat availability, and respond quickly to changes. These challenges highlight the need for a secure, scalable, and centralized event management solution like EVENTHUB.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
602 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 270 0 R
/E (Overall, these challenges reduce the efficiency and reliability of traditional event management approaches. Without proper security, scalability, and centralized control, existing systems fail to meet the demands of modern event organization. This creates a strong need for an improved and automated solution.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [2 3]
>>
endobj
603 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 270 0 R
/E (The proposed system, EVENTHUB, aims to overcome the limitations of the existing system by providing a secure and centralized web-based event management platform. The system automates essential processes such as event creation, user registration, and ticket booking through a single interface. By integrating frontend and backend technologies, EVENTHUB ensures smooth data flow and real-time updates. This approach significantly reduces manual effort and improves accuracy in event management operations.The modular architecture allows efficient handling of multiple user requests and real-time data processing. EVENTHUB also ensures consistent system reliability by maintaining structured data flow between the frontend, backend, and database.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
604 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 270 0 R
/E (Furthermore, the proposed system implements role-based access control and secure authentication mechanisms to ensure the protection of sensitive user and event data. Administrators are granted exclusive privileges to create, update, and manage event details, monitor registrations, and control ticket availability, while general users are restricted to viewing events and booking tickets based on availability. This clear separation of roles helps prevent unauthorized access and reduces the risk of data manipulation. Secure authentication mechanisms are incorporated to validate user identities and safeguard login credentials.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
endobj
