/P 277 0 R
/E (The system architecture of EVENTHUB follows a three-tier structure comprising the presentation layer, application layer, and database layer for better scalability and maintainability. The presentation layer is built using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript to provide user interfaces for administrators and users to manage and book events. The application layer uses Node.js and Express.js to handle business logic, RESTful APIs, authentication, and role-based access control.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
685 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 277 0 R
/E (The EVENTHUB system incorporates multiple security mechanisms to protect user data, event information, and booking records from unauthorized access and misuse. Authentication is implemented using JSON Web Tokens \(JWT\), ensuring that only verified users and administrators can access protected APIs and perform sensitive operations such as event creation, modification, and booking management. Role-based access control \(RBAC\) is enforced at the application layer to clearly separate admin and user privileges, preventing normal users from accessing administrative functionalities. All communication between the client and server is performed over HTTP or can be upgraded to HTTPS in deployment to safeguard credentials and session tokens from interception.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
