/P 278 0 R
/E (The EVENTHUB system can be deployed in multiple environments to ensure flexibility, scalability, and ease of maintenance. During development and testing, the application runs on a local machine using Node.js for the backend and a local PostgreSQL instance, allowing developers to verify features and fix issues quickly. For production, EVENTHUB can be hosted on a cloud platform such as AWS or similar providers, where the Node.js server runs on a virtual machine or managed service and the database is hosted using a managed relational database service. Containerization tools like Docker can be used to package the application and its dependencies into portable images, ensuring consistent behavior across different machines and simplifying deployment. )
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [7 8]
>>
endobj
