766 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 283 0 R
/E (The proposed EVENTHUB system introduces a streamlined, web-based methodology designed to replace outdated and inefficient event management practices with a centralized digital platform. Instead of depending on manual registration, paper forms, or scattered spreadsheets, the system uses structured web forms, secure authentication, and automated booking workflows to handle event-related operations end to end. Its methodology combines real-time data updates, role-based access control, and a responsive user interface so that both organizers and participants can interact with the platform efficiently and reliably. Together, these components ensure that event organizers maintain continuous visibility over registrations, capacity, and basic booking status, reducing coordination issues and improving overall event experience)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
767 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 283 0 R
/E (At the core of this methodology is a full-stack architecture built using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript on the frontend, with Node.js and Express.js managing the backend services. The backend exposes RESTful APIs for functionalities such as user registration, login, event creation, event listing, and ticket booking, while JSON-based communication ensures lightweight and consistent data exchange between client and server. Authentication and authorization are implemented using JSON Web Tokens \(JWT\), allowing the system to validate users securely and enforce separate privileges for administrators and normal users. This design keeps the application responsive and scalable, making it suitable for environments where the number of events and users may grow over time, such as college festivals or institutional programs.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
768 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 283 0 R
/E (Complementing the core logic is a relational database \(such as PostgreSQL\) that stores users, events, and booking records in well-structured tables, ensuring data integrity and easy retrieval. Each booking operation updates event capacity and generates a persistent record, enabling organizers to review participation levels, manage cancellations, and prevent overbooking. Additional modules, such as image upload for event posters and optional integration with payment gateways or email notifications, can be layered on top of this foundation without changing the core workflow.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [6 7]
>>
endobj
