/P 290 0 R
/E (Future enhancements for the EVENTHUB system focus on improving usability, expanding automation, and enabling wider deployment across institutions and organizations. Advanced analytics modules can be added to generate reports on event attendance, popular categories, and user engagement, helping organizers make data-driven decisions for future planning. Integration with online payment gateways and automated email/SMS notifications will further streamline the booking process by enabling instant payment confirmation, reminders, and digital tickets.)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
836 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 290 0 R
/E (The EVENTHUB project demonstrates how a well-designed full-stack web application can modernize event management by replacing fragmented manual processes with a unified, automated platform. Through its secure authentication, structured workflows, and real-time updates, the system improves reliability for organizers and convenience for participants in academic and organizational settings. Beyond fulfilling academic requirements, the project provides practical exposure to end-to-end software development, from requirements analysis and architecture design to implementation and testing, thereby strengthening technical and problem-solving skills)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
837 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 290 0 R
/E (This project successfully implements a secure and scalable web-based event management system that digitizes core processes such as event creation, user registration, and ticket booking through a centralized platform. By integrating a full-stack architecture using HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Node.js, Express.js, and a relational database, the system overcomes limitations of traditional manual and spreadsheet-based methods, reducing human errors and improving coordination between organizers and participants. Role-based authentication with JWT and structured database management ensure that user and event data are handled securely while maintaining reliable performance for multiple events and users. The developed prototype demonstrates how modern web technologies can streamline event organization, enhance user experience, and provide a strong foundation for further extensions such as payments, notifications, and analytics.)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
